flowchart TD
    A[Conceptual decision: consider response chunking] --> B{Is delivery the measured bottleneck?}
    B -->|No| C[Keep current delivery; investigate the measured stage]
    B -->|Yes| D{Can producer and receiver share the envelope contract?}
    D -->|No| E[Keep full-buffer behavior or design an adapter first]
    D -->|Yes| F{Does serialized payload meet the configured threshold?}
    F -->|No| G[Small-path API behavior: AdaptiveResponseFilter returns full result; filter_response yields one concat envelope]
    F -->|Yes| H{Can each emitted chunk fit the byte cap without splitting UTF-8 code points?}
    H -->|No| I[Reject explicitly; revise payload shape or cap]
    H -->|Yes| J{Does receiver support merge mode, stable total_chunks, and one-message state?}
    J -->|No| E
    J -->|Yes| K[Use bounded CRC32 envelopes and complete reassembly]
    K --> L[Add transport retries, timeouts, and UI policy separately]
    I -. edge case: chunking must preserve valid UTF-8 and reject unsplittable values .-> J
    J -. contract guard: conflicting duplicate frames, total metadata drift, changing total_chunks mid-message, and single-message reuse are rejected; identical duplicates are ignored .-> K
